            "paragraph": "This research examines the ability of CMIP6 decadal climate predictions to represent subregional climate conditions in the Emilia-Romagna region of northern Italy. The objective is to assess whether these predictions are sufficient to support regional-scale climate analyses relevant to water-resource-dependent sectors. The Emilia-Romagna region is characterized by diverse microclimates, shaped by its geographical setting and proximity to both the Mediterranean Sea and the Apennine Mountains. This leads to substantial spatial variability in climate patterns, highlighting the need for fine-resolution analyses. To capture these local-scale dynamics, the analysis is conducted at a spatial resolution of 0.05\u00b0 and focuses on assessing and correcting drift in precipitation and temperature using data from ten realizations of the Met Office Hadley Centre (MOHC) HadGEM3-GC31-MM model (Williams et al. 2018), a contributor to the CMIP6-DCPP initiative.",
            "ontology_conformed": false,
            "evidence_validated": true,
